    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Predicate returning true for matching names.</para><para>Returns true if and only if the final component of the path matches the specified regular expression.</para><para>For example, to find all files whose base name matches the glob &quot;rose_*&quot; use this (note that the corresponding regular expression is &quot;rose_.*&quot;, with a dot):</para><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">using<sp/>namespace<sp/>Rose::FileSystem;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Path<sp/>top<sp/>=<sp/>&quot;/foo/bar&quot;;<sp/>//<sp/>where<sp/>the<sp/>search<sp/>starts</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">std::vector&lt;Path&gt;<sp/>roseFiles<sp/>=<sp/>findAllNames(top,<sp/>baseNameMatches(boost::regex(&quot;rose_.*&quot;)));</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>    </detaileddescription>
